{"event": "agent", "step": 187, "message": {"type": "bug_report", "element": "Upcoming recurring payment row in the history list's \"subscriptions outside of the period\" section", "element_ref": 18, "expected": "Each upcoming recurring payment entry should show when it is due (its scheduled date, e.g. \"13 Dec\" for Rent and \"14 Dec\" for SkipTest/GymSub), because these entries are outside any date section and therefore the date is not shown anywhere else.", "observed": "The upcoming recurring entries only show a time-of-day (\"Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM\", \"Recurrent expense — 08:14 AM\", \"Recurrent expense — 08:10 AM\") with no due date. The Subscriptions screen shows these three are due on different dates (Rent Dec 13, SkipTest Dec 14, GymSub Dec 14), but the history entries give no date, so they look like they are all due at those times today.", "observed_quote": "Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM", "screen": "Expense history list (Today screen > history sheet, \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\")", "steps": ["Open the expense history list from the Today screen.", "Tap \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" to reveal the upcoming recurring payments.", "Observe the entries: Rent / \"Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM\" / $20, SkipTest / \"Recurrent expense — 08:14 AM\" / $2, GymSub / \"Recurrent expense — 08:10 AM\" / $3.", "None of the entries shows a due date - only the time. Compare with Analytics > Subscriptions (tap the \"1 Recurrent Expense\" card), which lists Rent as due \"In 4 weeks (Dec 13)\" and SkipTest/GymSub as due \"In 4 weeks (Dec 14)\".", "So in the history's subscriptions section the user cannot tell when each upcoming recurring payment will actually be charged."], "symptom_type": "missing", "anchor_node": {"text": "Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM", "class": "android.widget.TextView", "bounds": [84, 1521, 542, 1560]}}}
