{"event": "agent", "step": 247, "message": {"type": "bug_report", "element": "History date section heading for the 12 November group", "element_ref": 16, "expected": "Per the change in this build, date section headings should be formatted with the weekday name. 12 November 2026 is a Thursday (confirmed by the app's own date picker: \"Thursday, November 12, 2026\"), so the heading should read something like \"Thursday, 12 November\" / \"Thu, 12 Nov\".", "observed": "The section heading shows only \"12 November\" - the weekday name is missing. The same is true for the 13 November section (\"13 November\", which the date picker confirms is Friday, November 13, 2026). No history section heading anywhere on the screen contains a weekday name.", "observed_quote": "12 November", "screen": "Expense history list (Today screen, bottom sheet pulled into the history position)", "steps": ["Open the expense history list: from the Today/keypad screen drag the bottom sheet into the history position (the list starts with the $100 Total budget card, 11 Nov -> 04 Dec).", "The list has date section headings. The first is \"Today\", then \"13 November\" (Groceries $40), then \"12 November\" (Coffee $5).", "Read the 12 November heading: it is exactly \"12 November\" with no weekday name before it.", "Cross-check the weekday with the app's own date picker: expand the Coffee entry, tap Edit, tap \"Change date\" - the picker labels the day as \"Thursday, November 12, 2026\" (and 13 Nov as \"Friday, November 13, 2026\").", "Therefore the new weekday-name formatting is not applied to any history section heading; they show day+month only."], "symptom_type": "missing", "anchor_node": {"class": "android.view.View", "contains": ["Expand", "12 November", "$5"], "bounds": [42, 1392, 1038, 1489]}}}
